From f56c6d2d41ca9584ec515b07bbce4fded46676ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Prateek <prateekxd15@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:42:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(live): ingest and score chat replays for long streams

Add backend/src/live/chat_replay.py:
- fetch_youtube_chat(url, out_dir) runs yt-dlp with --write-subs
  --sub-langs live_chat and returns the downloaded .live_chat.json, or
  None when a stream kept no replay.
- fetch_twitch_chat(url, out_dir) uses TwitchDownloaderCLI only when it is
  on PATH, otherwise None. The CLI is not bundled.
- load_messages(path) normalises both formats to [(t_sec, author, text)],
  skipping engagement notices and records without a video offset.

Add backend/src/live/chat_signals.py:
- chat_series(messages, duration) -> {"rate", "unique", "hype"} per second;
  hype is the share of a second's messages carrying LUL/KEKW/OMEGALUL/
  LMAO/LOL, the laugh/skull/fire emoji (or their yt-dlp :shortcut: names),
  a lone W/L, a run of question marks, or an all-caps message.
- chat_zscores(series, params) reuses selection.causal_z, so a burst is
  compared with the minutes before it, not with the whole stream.

Nothing is wired into vod.py, selection.py or a route yet. Verified on
three real long YouTube streams with chat replay: 9,527 / 560 / 36,323
messages; the top hype seconds are in the round-4 report.

Co-Authored-By: DeepSeek V4.1 Flash Free <noreply@deepseek.com>
